NOTE ON THE NAMESPACING FIX (what I changed and why)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
First full build surfaced that my initially generic TirePressure* type names duplicated the committed
TirePressureHistoryWidget's generic types (TirePressureUnit/Connection/LoadStatus/Update/Projection/
Strings/Telemetry/Accessibility + InMemoryTirePressureSource/OSLogTirePressureTelemetry). I renamed ALL my
types to the unique TirePressureSection* namespace (the same collision-avoidance convention the sibling
TemperatureSection uses with TempSection*). Post-rename: my surface compiles with zero errors AND the two
committed Tire widgets are unambiguous again. The public surface name `TirePressureSection`, the diagnostics
slug "TirePressureSection", and the strings table "TirePressureSection" are unchanged.

